  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation per RBC-TOC-02 for 5 patients. Each has a progress note, and three have an update note for new results that arrived while I worked.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide raised to 40 mg BID (mr-t0001). The signed addendum overrides the summary's \"40 mg daily\".\n- KCl stopped (mr-00076).\n- Omeprazole kept. Pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution and was not ordered.\n- Lisinopril: I first kept it on hold because K was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat BMP on 10/23 showed K 4.7 and SCr 1.21, so I resumed it (mr-00072).\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg BID came in. It was not acted on.\n- FLAG: task-t0003 (recheck K before resuming lisinopril) is no longer needed. I couldn't close it from my side, so please close it (message comm-t0022).\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol: changed to 12.5 mg BID per the summary. A signed addendum then reversed this (HR 48–52), so he is back on 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0016).\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 unchanged.\n- FLAG: atorvastatin fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission (last fill 03/04). No change made; messaged you.\n- FLAG: glipizide 5 mg from an outside prescriber (Dr. Desai, Lakeview Drug) is not in the discharge summary and has no clinic order. Not ordered; messaged you.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril: resumed because SCr was 1.08 (10/22). Then a K of 5.5 came in from 10/23, so it is back on hold (mr-00373).\n- FLAG: task-t0018 (due 10/27) asks you to review the next potassium before resuming lisinopril.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge SCr 1.12 and K 4.4.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067)\n- Metformin ER stays on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, and the instruction requires a post-discharge result.\n- FLAG: task-t0013 (due 10/24) asks you to review the post-discharge BMP and resume metformin if SCr < 1.5.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nAll 4 inbox items that arrived during the work are completed. Fill coverage was at least 80% for everything except Terence Stark's atorvastatin.",
